From: Cristian Papa <pcristian292@gmail.com>
Subject: net: airoha: xpon: per-GEM MIB counters

The GPON MAC keeps RX/TX frame and payload byte counters for every valid
GEM port, read through an indirect command window (0x120-0x128) and
mapped by a GEM-ID group index table (0x140-0x148). Track the GEM ports
valid in hardware, rebuild the index table synchronously whenever that
set changes (the vendor driver waits 2 s, counting into shifted rows
meanwhile), fold the counts into 64-bit software totals every 5 s and
expose them in sysfs as gpon_gem_mib.

The register side is off by default: it starts when 1 is written to
gpon_gem_mib_enable, so the default datapath never touches the MIB
tables. The sequence follows the stock xpon.ko (gponDevGetGemPortCounter,
gponDevUpdateGemMibIdxTable), without its read-and-clear path and its
poll of the wrong done register.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
